{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1467284-importing-the-coalition-from-trinity-aeon-into-the-cofd-as-deviant-antagonists","id":1467284,"title":"Importing the Coalition from Trinity: Aeon into the CofD as Deviant antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-09T13:08:35-08:00","id":1467284,"title":"Importing the Coalition from Trinity: Aeon into the CofD as Deviant antagonists","content":"Because why not? The biopunk invaders and their myriad sympathetic slaves are a living horror trope, that of the all-devouring colonialists.<br /> <br /> For those of you not from the other boards, the Coalition is a spacefaring collective of species that is actually one race, the Progenitors, and the various servant phyles they made to run their generation Ark ships (all-rounder drones, spy/diplomat envoys, engineer sasqs, and space marine spinals). They are also ravenous planet looters; when they find a life-bearing world, they strip-mine it for both resources to upgrade the Arks and genetic traits to enhance new generations of the phyles. While not inherently evil, the Progenitors are pretty much irredeemable as a culture, and they have a distinct ability to emotion-control others with their pheromones (other phyles have variants, so a spinal is literally radiating terror and sasqs can make smellogram post-it notes, but Progenitors have outright compliance scents). A spaceborne Web of Pain.<br /> <br /> Actually, I only plan on a large scouter ship of theirs being crashed on Earth to be picked over by the Web of Pain, and later cloning their component phyles as servants to fake an alien invasion (this plot is very much a less gruesome version of Hostile Waters; the idea is that the Web creates a fake danger to rescue the world from, only for their cloned Progenitors to show they're a lot more instinctively adept at genetic engineering and revolt, seeking to contact their ancestral Ark with an SOS and provoke a real invasion if their attempt to phone home isn't stopped). <br /> <br /> So, how would you represent them, and their distinct BO?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T13:47:02-08:00","id":1467290,"title":"","content":"I mean, to represent controlling people's emotions with pheromones, probably I'd use the Pheromones Variation that controls people's emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T15:37:56-08:00","id":1467296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/146728